##

00:00:00.097 --> 00:00:01.880 position:72% line:85%
I invited some friends to play games in a pub.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.141 line:91%
No big prizes, just bragging rights
and the end card of the video.

00:00:05.141 --> 00:00:08.022 position:72% line:91%
Joining me this time are
Sophie Ward from science channel <i>Soph's Notes</i>,

00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:10.590 line:91%
musician dodie,
stand-up mathematician Matt Parker,

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.505 position:56% line:91%
and a charging cable that got caught
in the 360 camera shot,

00:00:13.505 --> 00:00:15.911 line:91%
and which we're just gonna
have to deal with.

00:00:19.876 --> 00:00:21.777 line:85%
Sophie, dodie, Matt,

00:00:21.777 --> 00:00:24.309 line:91%
thank you very much for
joining me in the pub.

00:00:24.309 --> 00:00:27.532 line:91%
The game is <i>No Thanks!</i>,
and here's how it's played.

00:00:27.532 --> 00:00:31.161 line:91%
<i>There's a deck of cards with
every number between 3 and 35.</i>

00:00:31.161 --> 00:00:35.161 position:66% line:91%
<i>But for each game, nine of those cards
have been removed from the deck at random.</i>

00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:38.183 position:58% line:91%
<i>In each round, a card is turned over,
and each player in turn can either</i>

00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:40.403 line:91%
<i>place a token on it
and pass it on to the next player,</i>

00:00:40.403 --> 00:00:43.335 line:91%
<i>or take the card
and all the tokens on it.</i>

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:46.501 line:91%
<i>If you have no tokens left,
you must take the card.</i>

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.734 line:91%
<i>Once all the cards have been taken,
the game ends.</i>

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:51.811 line:91%
<i>Each player's score is the sum of
the numbers on their cards,</i>

00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:56.360 position:63% line:91%
<i>less one point for each token they have,
and the lowest score wins.</i>

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.840 position:81% line:91%
<i>So cards are bad and tokens are good,
but they're not gonna be able to pass on every card.</i>

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.656 line:85%
<i>And there is one other rule:</i>

00:01:02.656 --> 00:01:08.222 position:69% line:91%
<i>If they've got a stack of consecutive cards,
only the lowest of that stack counts.</i>

00:01:08.918 --> 00:01:13.357 line:85%
Right! I mean, who's starting...?

00:01:13.357 --> 00:01:14.853 line:85%
Cool, I'll start!

00:01:15.496 --> 00:01:17.948 position:58% line:91%
<c.green>Oh wait, should we hide our counters?</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yes, hide your counters.</c>

00:01:17.948 --> 00:01:19.826 line:91%
<c.green>I have to give it a...</c>
<c.yellow>This wasn't even the highest yet.</c>

00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:21.826 line:91%
Oh, that's true. You have eleven,
we all have eleven count.

00:01:21.826 --> 00:01:23.678 line:91%
<c.yellow>Everyone can count.</c>
<c.green>Oh, do you(?)</c>

00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:27.381 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Huh. Um...</c>
<c.green>Oh, okay.</c>

00:01:27.381 --> 00:01:29.127 line:91%
<c.yellow>Oh.</c>
<c.cyan>Alright, well...</c>

00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:31.911 line:91%
I mean, I'm just gonna take the 3.
I'm just gonna have that.

00:01:31.911 --> 00:01:33.510 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>What's your advantage of taking that?</c>

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.657 position:63% line:85%
If I take— If I put a counter on that...

00:01:36.657 --> 00:01:37.960 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah?</c>

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.470 line:91%
...you can take it and get
a grand total of two points.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.791 line:85%
<c.yellow>Ah, so you were just stopping me...</c>

00:01:41.791 --> 00:01:44.441 line:91%
I'm stopping you going,
"I'll have that and the counter."

00:01:44.441 --> 00:01:46.430 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>You'd rather take a 3...</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>I'd rather take a hit of three points...</c>

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.957 line:91%
<c.yellow>...than give me a 2.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>...than give you—</c>

00:01:47.957 --> 00:01:52.908 position:73% line:91%
I'd rather take the hit of three than
you take two points and get one of my counters.

00:01:52.908 --> 00:01:53.986 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>That's a big deal.</c>
<c.yellow>Okay, okay.</c>

00:01:53.986 --> 00:01:57.701 position:63% line:91%
<c.cyan>It literally says on the card,
"Great! I'm the best! Pick me, take me!"</c>

00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:00.538 line:85%
18, that can go around the table.

00:02:00.538 --> 00:02:02.538 line:85%
<c.yellow>You have no interest in 18?</c>

00:02:02.538 --> 00:02:06.178 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>We'll see how many...</c>
<c.yellow>Okay, okay. Interesting.</c>

00:02:06.178 --> 00:02:09.646 line:91%
There is an advantage to having
some high cards in front of you,

00:02:09.646 --> 00:02:12.179 position:56% line:91%
because then other cards get cheaper
if the next one comes up.

00:02:12.179 --> 00:02:13.773 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>So... alright.</c>
<c.green>Okay, yeah.</c>

00:02:13.773 --> 00:02:16.035 line:85%
<c.green>That's a lot of chocolate buttons!</c>

00:02:17.589 --> 00:02:19.334 line:85%
I'll send it around one more.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.288 line:85%
Or...

00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:23.346 line:91%
I probably shouldn't say
my strategy out loud.

00:02:23.346 --> 00:02:25.209 line:85%
<c.green>Oh no, please Tom.</c>

00:02:27.352 --> 00:02:31.249 line:91%
<c.yellow>What we could do is add a token,
and then we could slide it on.</c>

00:02:31.249 --> 00:02:33.767 position:69% line:91%
<c.cyan>I thought we were gonna physically slide it.</c>
<c.yellow>And then you can say thanks or no thanks.</c>

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:34.809 line:85%
Yeah.

00:02:34.809 --> 00:02:37.395 line:91%
<c.green>Delicious. Yum-yum-yum.
I'm gonna take it.</c>

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.394 position:56% line:85%
So it's a hit of 12 points in total,

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:45.562 position:64% line:91%
but you've now got a load of counters
that you can throw away other cards with.

00:02:45.562 --> 00:02:47.593 line:85%
So you pick the next card.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.948 line:91%
<c.green>Wow.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Second highest card in the game.</c>

00:02:51.948 --> 00:02:54.283 line:91%
<c.green>Pretty big. I'm gonna put
a wee counter on that.</c>

00:02:54.283 --> 00:02:58.088 position:69% line:91%
<c.cyan>Yeah, I think I understand the game enough
to know I should put a counter down on that.</c>

00:02:58.088 --> 00:03:00.507 line:85%
Yeah, that's going round.

00:03:00.507 --> 00:03:02.197 line:85%
<c.yellow>No thanks(!)</c>

00:03:02.197 --> 00:03:05.290 position:66% line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>You don't have to say it. The rules say...</c>
<c.yellow>But I can!</c>

00:03:06.469 --> 00:03:08.948 line:91%
<c.yellow>There's no rule that says you're
not allowed to say it every time.</c>

00:03:08.948 --> 00:03:10.097 line:85%
<c.cyan>Okay...</c>

00:03:10.097 --> 00:03:12.696 line:85%
<c.green>I don't have a good gauge of...</c>

00:03:12.696 --> 00:03:15.908 line:91%
<c.green>Surely like half, right?</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>I don't know, 'cause...</c>

00:03:15.908 --> 00:03:19.090 line:91%
'Cause the advantage of taking that
is if 33 or 35 come up,

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.673 line:85%
you are in such a strong position.

00:03:20.673 --> 00:03:23.703 position:58% line:91%
<c.cyan>Ooh, right, yeah.</c>
<c.green>Yeah, 'cause then you got loads of...</c>

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.357 line:85%
<c.cyan>Right, yeah.</c>

00:03:25.357 --> 00:03:26.645 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah, I'm taking it.</c>

00:03:26.645 --> 00:03:27.985 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Alright.</c>
<c.yellow>Thanks!</c>

00:03:27.985 --> 00:03:30.707 line:91%
<c.green>Wow!</c>
<c.cyan>Ooh, okay.</c>

00:03:30.707 --> 00:03:33.425 line:85%
I was going to, if he didn't, so...

00:03:33.425 --> 00:03:34.995 line:85%
<c.cyan>Yeah, well— Okay, okay.</c>

00:03:34.995 --> 00:03:37.119 line:91%
'Cause now I'm starting to get
a little bit antsy

00:03:37.119 --> 00:03:39.605 position:78% line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>about how many counters I've got.</c>
<c.cyan>My hand's a bit light, isn't it? It's a bit light.</c>

00:03:39.605 --> 00:03:42.134 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>It literally says "I'm a loser" on it.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yes, it does.</c>

00:03:42.134 --> 00:03:46.439 line:91%
<c.yellow>A little passive-aggressive
for a play piece in the game.</c>

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:48.013 line:85%
<c.yellow>Being heckled by the—</c>

00:03:48.013 --> 00:03:50.602 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Oh no!</c>
<c.cyan>Oh, no!</c>

00:03:50.602 --> 00:03:51.947 line:91%
<c.cyan>What?!</c>
<c.yellow>35...</c>

00:03:51.947 --> 00:03:54.318 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Those cards were thoroughly shuffled.</c>
<c.yellow>...how I love you.</c>

00:03:54.318 --> 00:03:57.409 line:91%
<c.yellow>You know, if you love something,
you set it free.</c>

00:03:57.409 --> 00:04:00.376 line:91%
<c.yellow>So I'm gonna...</c>
<c.cyan>No, you're not!</c>

00:04:00.376 --> 00:04:03.403 line:91%
<c.yellow>Go explore the world.
Come back to me...</c>

00:04:03.403 --> 00:04:06.621 position:72% line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>'Cause you know you're never gonna get the 34.</c>
<c.yellow>...when you're ready to settle down.</c>

00:04:07.264 --> 00:04:09.164 line:85%
<c.green>Well, I don't want it!</c>

00:04:09.164 --> 00:04:10.716 line:85%
<c.green>"Oh, no!"</c>

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:14.118 line:91%
