00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:17.717 line:91%
<c.yellow>The only thing I love more than
sequential numbers is palindromes.</c>

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:20.694 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Oh god damn it, Matt!</c>
<c.yellow>So... I'll take that.</c>

00:05:20.694 --> 00:05:23.773 line:91%
<c.yellow>Add these to the bank.</c>
<c.green>I don't know how many—</c>

00:05:23.773 --> 00:05:26.291 line:91%
<c.yellow>A sting of regret, even though
you made the wrong decision.</c>

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.398 line:85%
Yeah. Alright, your card.

00:05:33.304 --> 00:05:36.480 position:61% line:91%
<c.cyan>Key to the door.
Oh no, it's not. It's not bingo, is it?</c>

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.560 position:61% line:85%
<c.yellow>There are little number facts on these.</c>

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.844 line:91%
<c.cyan>"Drop it like it's hot," it says.</c>
<c.yellow>"Double down."</c>

00:05:41.344 --> 00:05:42.674 line:85%
<c.green>I'm in the majority.</c>

00:05:42.674 --> 00:05:46.196 position:72% line:91%
<c.yellow>This is a missed opportunity,
'cause they could have facts about the number.</c>

00:05:46.196 --> 00:05:48.020 line:91%
<c.yellow>And they've got words
that rhyme with the number.</c>

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.130 line:91%
<c.green>Do you have any facts
about that number?</c>

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.786 line:85%
<c.yellow>A palindromic prime.</c>

00:05:51.786 --> 00:05:55.836 line:85%
I really need some counters.

00:05:55.836 --> 00:05:58.202 position:67% line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>And if I don't take this—</c>
